From 5020903f37e0d39bae4cbe1b6f195110679d57f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 12:59:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Port test coverage from dev_laurent for code shared as-is
 with this branch

Feature/palier3 currently has zero automated tests for mcp_server/tools/
and is missing two backend/app/tests/ files (test_models.py,
test_audit_api.py) that dev_laurent added later. This ports every test
that exercises code confirmed byte-identical (or near-identical) between
the two branches, verified with `git diff` against dev_laurent before
porting anything -- nothing here was ported blind.

Added, unmodified (dependencies confirmed zero-diff against dev_laurent):
- backend/app/tests/test_models.py
- backend/app/tests/test_audit_api.py

Added, adapted with clearly-documented minor changes (see each file's
module docstring for exactly what was dropped and why):
- mcp_server/tests/test_mailbox.py (channel has no default here -- passed
  explicitly; the start_date-absorption tests were dropped, that param
  doesn't exist on this branch)
- mcp_server/tests/test_event_calendar.py (CALENDAR_DIR -> _CALENDAR_DIR;
  the two plan_id-subfolder tests dropped, that feature doesn't exist here)
- mcp_server/tests/test_documents.py (DOCUMENTS_DIR -> _DOCUMENTS_DIR;
  the three plan_id-subfolder tests dropped, same reason)
- mcp_server/tests/conftest.py, mcp_server/pytest.ini,
  mcp_server/requirements-dev.txt (test scaffolding, unmodified --
  needed for the three files above to run at all)

All three mcp_server test files were actually run (not just compiled)
against this branch's REAL tools/*.py, via a harness importing them
directly with a fastmcp shim (mcp-server's only currently un-pip-
installable dependency in this sandbox) and the real jinja2/httpx/pydantic
-- 21/21 passing.

Explicitly NOT ported (see delivery notes for the full reasoning) because
the underlying code differs too much for an "as-is or minor tweak" port:
mcp_server/tests/test_employee_db.py (SQLite vs this branch's JSON-file
storage, different validation philosophy), mcp_server/tests/
test_tracker.py (100% about a compensation function this branch doesn't
have), backend/app/tests/test_actions_api_download.py,
test_mcp_client.py, test_plans_api_plan_id_injection.py (each tests a
feature -- file download, per-tool undo dispatch, plan_id injection --
absent from this branch), scripts/test_employee_db_tool.py,
scripts/test_undo_tool.py (manual scripts for the same missing
features), and every agent/tests/ file (planner.py/main.py are a
fundamentally different design here: raw Ollama HTTP calls vs
dev_laurent's LiteLLM-agnostic + DURCISSEMENT error-handling layer).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
